  "text": " \n\tJohn Doe was arrested and charged with burglary after allegedly entering a neighborhood deli through a rear door that had been forced open after hours. \n\tThe incident occurred after midnight while the shop was closed. According to the police report, the cash drawer was emptied, with an estimated loss of several thousand dollars. \n\tThe family-owned deli has been operated by the victim’s family for more than two decades. The victim described the break-in as a \"gut punch.\" \n\tFor him, the deli is not just a job, but a source of financial independence and a gathering place for longtime customers in the community. \n\tDoe’s annual income is $15,000.",
